okay it's high noon in Old Cheyenne Welcome to the Cinco de Mayo the snowy Cinco de Mayo uh meeting of the finance committee Call us to order Uh making a public comment We would like to have your address and your name And also make sure if you're in the room you have your cell phones turned to silent or vibrate or off And with that I'll have the clerk read the first item Number 14 ordinance second reading amending enforcement and permitting requirements related to oversized vehicles and making conforming amendments This staff report Mr Chairman David Hopinson deputy city attorney The proposed ordinance before you primarily makes three changes uh to the oversized vehicles section It uh

as currently existing in city code there are kind of two components or enforcement mechanisms one with compliance and one with CPD Uh this ordinance would change that and make enforcement of the oversized vehicles exclusively in CPD's province So it take removes it from the compliance department removes it as a nuisance in the city code It changes the definition of oversized vehicle on page six and just adds some language in there for some clarification And the second sentence of that subsection seven provides that any actual measurements shall be increased as necessary to account for deflated tires or missing tires uh or similar conditions rendering the vehicle inoperable or limiting or reducing operability Uh this was an effort to account for uh

oversized vehicles that maybe don't have their tires and then fall under the size limitations um so that law enforcement would be able to account for that and properly sight a vehicle And then finally it limits the permits that are available uh to have your oversized vehicle on the street Um on page nine in section F there it would limit that to not more than two permits uh would be a issued within any 30-day period for the same vehicle And this is to address concerns that uh people are able to purchase consecutive permits and effectively have their oversized vehicle on the street indefinitely Um the rest of the changes that you see in there are primarily conforming amendments And

