which calculated uh the total budget amount to be $30,000 above what it was actually approved Um so there was a line item 708 event management that the DDA decided to stripe from the budget Um unfortunately that was hidden instead of deleted Uh and then it was simply um in RXL added into the the total line item or the total budget Uh so that has been corrected for your approval Uh that means that the total budget is actually 1,22,800 which is only 196,526 more than the fiscal year 2026 final budget With that correction I'll run through a couple of highlights for this year's for the fiscal year 2027 budget As I stated the total proposed budget is 1,22,800 uh

an increase of approximately $196,500 from fiscal year 2026 final budget In terms of where the money comes from the largest revenue source is the MI levy assessment collections estimated at around $51,610 for this upcoming fiscal year This reflects a $14,600 increase from the fiscal year 2026 collections and we utilized a uh 3% CPI average annual increase year-over-year Uh $434,190 should be drawn uh from the reserves to fund strategic programs We also anticipate a $30,000 grant from the Cheyenne Larmy County Economic Development Joint Powers Board uh which is what we have received in the past or this past year as well as a $10,000 Laramie County grant for economic development The city is estimated to contribute about $290,900 to cover payroll benefits and

insurance for DDA staff This is not included in the DDA's uh operating and or administrative budget The largest part of the budget around 500,000 goes towards our three grant programs that we have This includes the facade impro improvement grant the capital improvement grant and the sidewalk match program The facade and capital improvement grants are allocated $200,000 each The uh the facade improvement is our preservation focus program um focusing on historic preservation of facades but also any other facade improvements we see downtown um the sighting windows things like that of that nature The capital improvement grant is our most utilized program and that can be used by both property and business owners or tenants within those properties for capital improvements such as signage benches and

anything in the right ofway The sidewalk match program has been allocated or has um has been allocated 100,000 for the fiscal year 2027 This was a pilot program started in 2024 and uh it is being formalized this year We're still working through the parameters with the city to ensure its effectiveness There are some bumps we need to work through The downtown planter program will receive 87,000 This covers our existing vendor contract through June 2027 and and it adds uh the eight water efficient planters for potentially the southside corridor or the west edge depending on how the summer 2026 pilot program goes Uh this also includes signage and winter displays Sponsorships are budgeted at 75,000 These are allocated on a request basis throughout the year to events that are free and

open to the public and have a direct community event Community events will will receive 125,000 Um and this is where that error occurred The event management prior of the prior years has been put into this line item This is a change from last year Uh the DDA is stepping back from coordinating events directly Uh this will cover events that we either annually support such as uh the Fridays on the plaza event the downtown holiday express shuttle uh busker program Cheyenne Day that Visit Cheyenne hosts um as well as events that we want to recruit to downtown such as the Wyoming Independent Film Festival that we're working on this summer We're also pro proposing a new line item This is a $10,000 contribution to Visit Cheyenne's shop local gift card program that they are starting to pilot this year This would be managed by Visit Cheyenne as part of the broader shop local initiative The board will work with visit Cheyenne to determine how participation is accessible to all

